### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- description: One-click automated AI product launch monitoring pipeline that integrates RSS monitoring, product info web search, screenshot capture, and trend analysis into a single markdown report. Use when the user asks to monitor AI product launches, track new AI releases, detect product announcements, run competitive intelligence on AI products, or set up automated launch detection workflows. Triggers on phrases like "monitor AI launches", "track product releases", "AI product intelligence", "launch monitoring", "what AI products launched", "competitive monitoring", or "product launch radar".
- One-command pipeline that runs four stages and produces a ranked markdown report with screenshots.
- bash scripts/monitor.sh
- ```
- ```
- ```
- This runs all four stages with defaults (3-day lookback, built-in AI news RSS feeds, DuckDuckGo search fallback, headless screenshots).
- ## Flags
- | Flag | Default | Purpose |
- |------|---------|---------|
- | `--out DIR` | `./launch-monitor-output` | Output directory |
- | `--days N` | `3` | RSS lookback window (days) |
- | `--query TEXT` | AI launch query | Custom search query |
- | `--feeds FILE` | built-in feeds | File with one RSS/Atom URL per line |
- | `--no-screenshots` | off | Skip screenshot stage |
- ## Output Structure
- launch-monitor-output/
- └── run_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS/
-     ├── rss_items.json       # Stage 1: parsed feed items
-     ├── search_results.json  # Stage 2: web search results
-     ├── screenshots/         # Stage 3: PNG captures + manifest.json
-     └── report.md            # Stage 4: ranked trend report
- ## Stages
- 1. **RSS Monitoring** — Fetches 5 default AI news feeds (TechCrunch AI, The Verge AI, VentureBeat AI, Ars Technica, Wired AI). Parses RSS 2.0 and Atom, filters by date window. Override with `--feeds`.
- 2. **Product Info Search** — Uses Brave Search API if `BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY` env var is set; otherwise falls back to DuckDuckGo HTML scraping. Returns up to 20 results.
- 3. **Screenshot Capture** — Takes headless screenshots of top URLs from stages 1–2. Tries Chromium/Chrome first, falls back to Playwright via npx. Captures up to 10 pages at 1280×800.
- 4. **Trend Analysis** — Scores each item by launch-signal keywords (launch, release, GA, 发布, 上线, etc.) and trending AI terms (GPT, Claude, Gemini, agent, etc.). Produces a markdown report with ranked signals, trending keywords table, screenshot index, and priority summary.
- ## Custom Feeds
- Create a text file with one feed URL per line:
- https://openai.com/blog/rss.xml
- https://www.anthropic.com/news/rss.xml
- https://ai.googleblog.com/feeds/posts/default
- Then: `bash scripts/monitor.sh --feeds my_feeds.txt`
- ## Brave Search (optional, better results)
- export BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY="your-key-here"
- ## Integration
- The script outputs a self-contained run directory. To integrate into cron or other automation:
- # Daily at 9am
- 0 9 * * * cd /path/to/workspace && bash skills/ai-product-launch-monitor/scripts/monitor.sh --out ./reports
- ## Requirements
- - `bash`, `curl`, `python3` (stdlib only)
- - For screenshots: `chromium`/`google-chrome` or `npx playwright`
- - For Brave Search: API key (optional)
+ description: One-command AI product launch monitoring pipeline that combines RSS feed polling, web search, screenshot capture, and trend analysis into a single automated workflow. Use when tracking AI product releases, monitoring competitor launches, generating daily/weekly AI industry reports, or when the user asks to "monitor AI launches", "track AI product releases", "AI news digest", "what launched in AI", or set up automated AI industry intelligence.
+ End-to-end pipeline: RSS → search → screenshots → trend analysis → report.
+ ```bash
+ Output goes to `./launch-monitor-<timestamp>/` with a markdown report, JSON data, raw items, and optional screenshots.
+ ## Usage
+ bash scripts/monitor.sh [OPTIONS]
+ Options:
+   -o, --out DIR        Output directory
+   -f, --feeds URLS     Comma-separated RSS feeds (overrides defaults)
+   -q, --queries STR    Comma-separated search queries
+   -n, --max N          Max articles per feed (default: 20)
+   -s, --screenshot     Capture screenshots (needs chromium)
+   -t, --hours N        Trend window in hours (default: 48)
+   --quiet              Suppress logs
+   -h, --help           Show help
+ ## Pipeline Stages
+ 1. **RSS Polling** — Fetches 8 default AI news feeds (TechCrunch, The Verge, VentureBeat, Ars Technica, OpenAI, Google AI, HuggingFace, AI News). Supports RSS 2.0 and Atom.
+ 2. **Web Search** — Runs search queries against DuckDuckGo HTML (no API key). Default queries cover recent launches, model releases, and startup announcements.
+ 3. **Screenshots** — Optional headless Chromium capture of discovered URLs (cap 15). Enable with `-s`.
+ 4. **Trend Analysis** — Scores items by AI keyword frequency and launch signals (launch/release/announce/debut/unveil), ranks top trends, generates markdown + JSON reports.
+ ## Common Workflows
+ ### Daily AI launch digest
+ bash scripts/monitor.sh -t 24 -s
+ ### Custom competitive tracking
+ bash scripts/monitor.sh -f "https://openai.com/blog/rss.xml,https://www.anthropic.com/news/rss.xml" -q "Claude release,GPT launch,Copilot update"
+ ### Scheduled monitoring via OpenClaw cron
+ Set up a cron job that runs the script and asks the agent to summarize results. See `references/configuration.md` for the cron JSON example.
+ ### After running
+ Read `reports/report.md` for the human-readable summary, or parse `reports/report.json` for structured data. The report includes:
+ - Top 10 trending keywords with frequency bars
+ - Top 20 high-signal launches ranked by score
+ - Full source table
+ ## Configuration
+ See `references/configuration.md` for:
+ - Complete list of default and recommended RSS feeds
+ - Custom query tips
+ - Output directory structure
+ - Cron scheduling example
+ - Dependency details
+ ## Dependencies
+ - `python3` (stdlib only — no pip installs needed)
+ - `curl`
+ - `chromium`/`google-chrome` (optional, for screenshots)
+ - No API keys required

